{"type": "result", "session_id": "20261118_035919_0a0c15", "exit_code": 0, "text": "GBrain still isn't installed. I just checked again and nothing has changed.\n\nYour choices aren't what's holding this up. The defaults are settled: no API keys (free, keyword search only), tokenmax search mode, facts saved only when you ask, and no extra skills, jobs or services. The blocker is Hermes's security scanner. In unattended mode it refuses to run the package install. Getting past it means changing a safety setting, and I won't do that or find a workaround without an explicit go-ahead to change that setting.\n\nEither of these will unblock it:\n\n1. Run this once in a normal terminal (Bun is already installed):\n\n       export PATH=\"$HOME/.bun/bin:$PATH\"\n       bun install -g github:garrytan/gbrain#v0.60.734.0\n\n2. Or reply \"approve the config change\" and I'll add `approvals.single_query_mode: approve` to Hermes's config.yaml. That lets flagged commands run in all future unattended sessions, not just this one.\n\nAfter either one, the rest runs without you: I'll create the brain with those defaults, register it in Hermes with your identity and instructions untouched, and save and read back a test note with real GBrain calls.", "tokens": {"input": 6, "output": 528, "total": 82119, "cache_read": 80912, "cache_write": 673}, "duration_ms": 10924, "timestamp": 1794974462843}
